@startuml SequenceDiagram_Facade
title Sequence Diagram — Facade Pattern\nFormMain calls simple GetAlbums(); FacebookManager hides all SDK complexity

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor White

actor "User" as User

participant ": FormMain"          as FM
participant ": FacebookManager"   as Facade
participant ": FacebookService"   as SDK
participant "loginResult : LoginResult" as LR
participant "user : User"         as U

note over FM, U
  FormMain never calls FacebookService, LoginResult,
  or user.Albums directly — it only calls FacebookManager.
  All SDK complexity is hidden behind simple method names.
end note

== Simple call: Login ==

User  ->  FM     : buttonConnectAsDesig_Click()
activate FM

FM    ->  Facade : ConnectWithToken(i_Token)
activate Facade

note over Facade
  Facade hides:
  - FacebookService.Connect()
  - null checks on LoginResult
  - token persistence (File.WriteAllText)
  - storing m_LoginResult
end note

Facade ->  SDK   : FacebookService.Connect(i_Token)
activate SDK
SDK   --> Facade : LoginResult
deactivate SDK

Facade ->  LR    : check AccessToken != null
activate LR
LR    --> Facade : valid
deactivate LR

Facade ->  Facade : m_LoginResult = loginResult\nFile.WriteAllText("token.txt", token)
Facade --> FM     : LoginResult
deactivate Facade

FM    ->  FM     : afterLogin()\ndisplayUserInfo()
deactivate FM

== Simple call: GetAlbums ==

User  ->  FM     : (after login — displayUserInfo)
activate FM

FM    ->  Facade : GetAlbums()
activate Facade

note over Facade
  Facade hides:
  - getting LoggedInUser from m_LoginResult
  - iterating user.Albums (SDK collection)
  - handling permission exceptions
  - converting to List<Album>
end note

Facade ->  Facade : user = LoggedInUser\n(from m_LoginResult)
Facade ->  U      : foreach album in user.Albums  [Graph API]
activate U
U     --> Facade  : Album objects
deactivate U

Facade --> FM     : List<Album>
deactivate Facade

FM    ->  FM     : listBoxAlbums.Items.Add(album.Name)
deactivate FM
@enduml
